WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.469 --> 00:00:05.380
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 7 is out,
let’s have a look.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.730
We meet Brother Ray, a priest who leads a
village somewhere in the riverlands.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
It seems a pretty nice place they’ve got
going – they’re working together to build

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:17.600
a sept, a seven-sided structure that serves
as a church of the Faith of the Seven.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.890
Brother Ray is similar to a book character
called the Elder Brother.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:24.929
He leads a group of monks who live on the
Quiet Isle, seeking atonement for their sins

00:00:24.929 --> 00:00:29.730
by taking vows of silence . Brienne visits
this island in the books, and there she sees

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.720
a certain monk digging graves.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.160
He’s unusually tall, and he limps as though
his leg was hurt , and he’s subtly associated

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.020
with dogs – so fans have speculated for
years that this gravedigger is the Hound.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:46.260
Remember, at the end of Season 4, Sandor is
beaten by Brienne, and left for dead by Arya

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:50.800
– but we never actually see him die, so
the theory is that he’s rescued by the Elder

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.900
Brother , and now lives on the Quiet Isle.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.480
And that’s basically what happens in the
show – Sandor’s saved by Ray, and now

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.510
lives among his people.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.870
In the books, it seems as though Sandor finds
peace in his new life , that he lets go of

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.600
hatred and violence – he actually becomes
one of the monks , atoning for his sins, though

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:12.030
in the show, Sandor says hate keeps him going
, he chops wood like he’s trying to murder

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:16.170
it, he seems pretty much unchanged from the
violent dude he was before.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:21.310
So maybe we’ll see change in his character
later – Ray says the gods have plans for

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.930
Sandor Clegane .
In King’s Landing, we see a very different

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.050
sort of priest.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:30.210
The High Sparrow visits Margaery, who’s
still acting all faithful and pious – she’s

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:33.340
also got a funny little crownlet cause Tyrells
do love their headwear.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.690
But they quote some scripture at each other,
and the Sparrow makes a comment that you don’t

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:41.150
have to know all the texts to be a good pious
person – which reflects on Ray, right?

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.960
He plays it pretty fast and loose with his
theology, says he doesn’t know much about

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.900
the gods, but nonetheless, he uses religious
ideas to help build a happy community.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.670
Game of Thrones shows that there are lots
of different ways to be religious, some good,

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.100
some bad, and most a bit of both.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.780
Anyway the Sparrow sits Marge down, gives
her a creepy priestly touch on the thigh,

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.670
and tells her she should be having more sex
with Tommen.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.280
It seems the Sparrow wants to make sure that
Tommen and Marge have a child, which of course

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.300
is very politically important, right?

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.560
A son of King Tommen would be the heir to
the Iron Throne, so maybe the Sparrow’s

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.890
making sure that his power through Tommen
will survive even if Tommen doesn’t.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:22.030
The Sparrow then subtly threatens Olenna so
Marge goes and visits her – with Septa Unella

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.270
watching over.

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:26.960
Marge talks the talk, acts like she’s on
the Sparrow’s side, but she secretly passes

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.090
a paper to Olenna with a drawing of a rose.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.760
This is refers to the sigil of House Tyrell,
what Marge is saying here is that while she

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.590
pretends to be all pious she’s truly still
on the side of Tyrell – so one of her goals

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.620
at this point may be to free her brother Loras.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:42.620
Somehow.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.810
Up north, Jon Snow tries to recruit the wildlings,
for his battle against the Boltons, and the

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:51.380
wildlings are in a terrible spot right now,
stuck between the northmen, who wanna kill

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:55.120
them, and the white walkers, who wanna kill
them then turn them into zombies.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.550
Jon argues that the wildlings’ best hope
is to side with the Starks and retake the

00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.550
north.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:03.160
Tormund argues that they owe Jon, cause he
saved them by letting them through the Wall.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.280
These are both strong arguments, so Jon gets
an endorsement from Wun Wun, and the wildlings

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.400
vote Snow.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.849
It is weird that, just a few episodes ago,
Tormund said the wildlings think that Jon

00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:15.781
Snow’s a god because he rose from the dead,
but for people who think he’s a god, they

00:03:15.781 --> 00:03:18.610
still need a lot of convincing to follow him.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:22.260
No one seems to think it’s a big deal anymore
that Jon was resurrected.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.400
Melisandre got all excited about it, said
Jon might be the prince that was promised,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.450
but we’ve barely seen her since.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:33.430
Jon himself seems unchanged by his resurrection,
his personality’s basically the same.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:38.160
What’s the point of killing then resurrecting
a character if that character doesn’t change

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.410
from the experience?

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:42.769
Hopefully we’ll get something more before
the season ends.

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:46.190
Back in King’s Landing, Cersei tries to
ally with Olenna, but the Queen of Thorns

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:50.200
tears her to shreds, points out that this
whole mess with the sparrows started because

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.709
Cersei allowed the Faith to arm themselves.

00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:56.990
Olenna suggests that Cersei might be “the
worst person [she’s] ever met”, and Cersei

00:03:56.990 --> 00:04:02.140
has done some terrible things – framing
the Tyrells, framing Tyrion, having King Robert

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.390
killed.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.180
Beating Ros, killing dwarfs, killing Lady.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.989
And that’s just in the show, she does even
worse in the books… not to mention her terrible

00:04:08.989 --> 00:04:13.019
political and economic decisions that damage
the whole realm… and that she’s just generally

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.930
cruel and horrible to the people around her.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:20.829
So some would call it justice that now, Cersei’s
lost everything – her power, her prestige,

00:04:20.829 --> 00:04:24.900
her father, her firstborn, her daughter…
in the books even her brother – and lover

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:25.990
– is slipping away.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:31.010
All Cersei has left now is Tommen, and he’s
in the hands of a scheming zealot.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:34.820
Really the only card Cersei’s still got
up her sleeve is the Mountain – so you can

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.720
be damn sure she’s gonna use him…

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:41.820
Jaime and Bronn arrive at Riverrun, which
is held by the “Blackfish”, Brynden Tully.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:45.950
The castle is under siege by the Freys, but
they aren’t doing a good job, so Jaime has

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:49.790
come to sort their shit out and take the castle
in the name of King Tommen.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.880
In the books, Jaime has a lot of complicated
feelings about this siege.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.180
For one thing, back in Book and Season 3 when
Cat releases him from captivity, she makes

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:01.940
him swear, on his honour and his family and
his gods, to “never again take up arms against

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.160
Stark nor Tully”.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:07.060
But unless Jaime can convince the Blackfish
to give up Riverrun peacefully, he’ll “need

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:10.030
to storm the castle” and break his oath.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:13.949
This affects how Jaime sees himself – he’s
known as the Kingslayer, “A man with shit

00:05:13.949 --> 00:05:18.680
for honor” , but he’s now trying to be
a better man, to keep his oaths.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.000
Another complication is the Blackfish himself.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.080
Brynden was a war hero back in the day, and
as a kid, Jaime idolised him, wanted to hear

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:30.530
all the stories of his exploits , but now,
Jaime is set against the man he once admired.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:35.090
Jaime’s been forced into a war against a
hero he looked up to, and against family he

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.910
swore never to attack.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:40.169
On top of that, he’s still reeling from
the loss of his hand, and the loss of his

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:45.060
father, which he feels he caused cause he
freed Tyrion, in the books he has a falling

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:49.500
out with Tyrion, and in the books Jaime starts
to break up with Cersei – basically Jaime’s

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:54.620
life has fallen apart, and this siege is the
stage where he starts to rebuild himself,

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:59.110
not as the douchey Prince Charming he was
before, but as a better nobler man.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.520
That’s what’s up in the books, anyway.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.600
Jon, Sansa and Davos arrive at Bear Island,
home of House Mormont.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.220
The Mormonts are a really cool family, their
leader was Jeor, until he went off to join

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.320
the Night’s Watch.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:16.150
Jeor left his son Jorah to rule, until he
got caught selling slaves and ran off to Essos,

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.260
where he ends up serving Daenerys.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:22.270
So Jeor’s sister Maege took charge, and
she’s this tough warrior woman type, who

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.490
fought alongside Robb Stark in his war.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:28.830
Maege has a bunch of daughters, warriors themselves,
and interestingly, it’s not clear who the

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:32.860
father of her children is, cause a husband
is never mentioned.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:37.820
But there is a theory – the wildling Tormund
seems to have a thing for warrior-women, right?

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.100
And he does claim to have fucked a she-bear.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:45.669
Maege’s nickname is “the She-Bear” , so
some fans believe Tormund and Maege may have

00:06:45.669 --> 00:06:50.110
had a secret romance, Tormund mighta taken
boats to Bear Island for booty calls.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:53.750
In show, though, Maege is now dead, as are
her elder daughters apparently, cause the

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.460
head of House Mormont is now ten-year-old
Lyanna.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:00.000
And she’s awesome – this tiny little kid
talking all big and stern.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.860
At first she’s reluctant to support the
Starks, because as she points out, Sansa and

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.360
Jon’s allegiance is questionable.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:10.380
Jon’s technically a Snow, not a Stark – at
least until we get news of his true parentage.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.449
And Sansa has been married to a Lannister
and a Bolton.

00:07:13.449 --> 00:07:17.470
In the end, what convinces Lyanna is Davos’
argument that they need to unite against the

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.470
white walkers.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:22.190
Which is a little puzzling – what does Lyanna
Stark know of white walkers?

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:27.430
Regardless, she gives Jon and Sansa the support
of her soldiers – all sixty-two of them.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:33.170
Just remember that if Lyanna meets Tormund,
she may unknowingly meet her father…

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:36.830
Back at Riverrun, Jaime goes and chats with
the Blackfish, and this goes down a lot like

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.240
it does in the books – Jaime tries to get
him to surrender, Blackfish talks a bunch

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:44.300
of smack – so it looks like Jaime will have
to attack Riverrun – and break his oath

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:45.419
to Catelyn.

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:49.560
However, things might change when Brienne
arrives – maybe some peaceful resolution

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.660
might be possible.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:56.360
The Starks go to speak to Lord Glover at Deepwood
Motte, and he flat-out refuses to support

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:57.360
them.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.289
He doesn’t want to fight alongside wildlings,
he doesn’t want to anger the Boltons, and

00:08:00.289 --> 00:08:04.630
he feels he was failed by the Starks under
Robb – remember Robb’s marriage to Talisa

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:11.520
screwed up the alliance with the Freys, which
led to Red Wedding, which led to the defeat

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:12.819
of north.

00:08:12.819 --> 00:08:16.530
Glover talks about the suffering of his family
during the war, and we’re reminded that

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:20.160
these struggles between Starks and Lannisters
and Tullys and Boltons don’t just affect

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:24.270
the lords and ladies at the top – they affect
the people who serve them, and those people

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:28.070
do have a right to be mad when they’re failed
by their overlords.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.319
Yara and Theon take a pit stop in Volantis.

00:08:30.319 --> 00:08:34.229
While Yara and her ironborn party it up, Theon
suffers.

00:08:34.229 --> 00:08:38.139
This episode is called “The Broken Man”,
but it could be called “The Broken Men”,

00:08:38.139 --> 00:08:42.379
look how many there are – Theon, Edmure,
Sandor and Gregor.

00:08:42.379 --> 00:08:44.860
Arguably Jaime, Jon, and Davos.

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:49.000
One of the great things about Game of Thrones
is that shows war has consequences, that people

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.769
get hurt in ways that don’t get better.

00:08:52.769 --> 00:08:57.209
Anyway Yara tells Theon to man up or die,
which is the ironborn approach to therapy,

00:08:57.209 --> 00:09:01.519
and Yara outlines her plan – to sail to
Meereen and ally with Daenerys so she can

00:09:01.519 --> 00:09:03.610
take back the Iron Islands.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:07.860
The question, of course, is whether Euron
can get there first.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.420
Back in the north, Davos and the Starks discuss
their situation.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:16.959
They’ve got 2000 wildlings, 200 Hornwoods,
143 Mazins, 42 Mormonts, and one Wun Wun which…

00:09:16.959 --> 00:09:22.470
isn’t enough to beat some 5000 Boltons , plus
however many Umbers and Karstarks they’ve

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:23.470
got.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:26.739
So Sansa writes a letter to Littlefinger asking
him to bring his knights of the Vale , which

00:09:26.739 --> 00:09:28.490
will probably make all the difference.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:32.170
It’s also possible that the Blackfish and
the Tullys might arrive to help, and there

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:35.869
are also the Manderlys – one of the largest
northern houses, that as far as we know, still

00:09:35.869 --> 00:09:37.379
hasn’t taken a side…

00:09:37.379 --> 00:09:41.329
However it turns out, this Battle of the Bastards
is gonna be huge.

00:09:41.329 --> 00:09:45.300
Back at the riverlands, three men come and
threaten Ray’s village, demanding horses

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:46.300
and food.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:50.300
They seem to be from the brotherhood without
banners, that outlaw group Arya meets in Season

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.300
3.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:55.339
The brotherhood is founded to protect the
common folk , and they do do some dodgy stuff,

00:09:55.339 --> 00:09:59.850
like stealing supplies from people, on a promise
to eventually pay them back . But these three

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:05.100
guys are acting like straight-up bandits,
and we soon see them do much worse…

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:09.360
In Braavos, Arya books a ship to take her
back to Westeros, then she goes for a walk,

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:10.910
and gets attacked by “the waif”.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.980
She escapes, but with a gut full of stab wounds.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.850
If this was any other character, you’d think
she’s gonna die, right?

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:21.110
But this is Arya – she’s been off on her
own storyline for ages, training for like

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:24.779
two seasons, there’s no way they’re gonna
suddenly kill her off now, and make her whole

00:10:24.779 --> 00:10:26.360
arc lead to nothing.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:28.420
So how’s she gonna survive?

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:32.649
It looks like she needs help, and right now,
Lady Crane is the closest thing Arya’s got

00:10:32.649 --> 00:10:37.230
to a friend in this city, so maybe Crane will
find her, somehow heal her, and send her on

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.860
her way to Westeros.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.240
It might be that simple.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:44.319
But there are a lot of crazy theories bout
more complicated ways this could go down.

00:10:44.319 --> 00:10:49.279
Like, some people think the waif is actually
a kinda split personality of Arya, like a

00:10:49.279 --> 00:10:54.439
Fight Club Tyler Durden type deal, or that
Arya used some acting tricks to fake her wounds

00:10:54.439 --> 00:10:55.720
with pig blood.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:11:00.089
They’re both cool ideas, but probably the
most likely crazy theory is the idea that

00:11:00.089 --> 00:11:02.079
that person who was stabbed isn’t Arya.

00:11:02.079 --> 00:11:06.499
Cause remember, we’re dealing with Faceless
assassins here, people who can magically take

00:11:06.499 --> 00:11:11.439
on the appearance of other people – so maybe
the person who was stabbed isn’t Arya, but

00:11:11.439 --> 00:11:12.439
Jaqen.

00:11:12.439 --> 00:11:17.309
Cause we have seen Jaqen wear Arya’s face
before, and we’ve seen Jaqen die for Arya

00:11:17.309 --> 00:11:21.629
before – he drinks poison so that Arya doesn’t
have to.

00:11:21.629 --> 00:11:25.389
The reason Jaqen’s still around is that
he’s not really a person, he’s no one,

00:11:25.389 --> 00:11:30.299
he’s just a face that can be worn by any
Faceless Man – it is confusing but the point

00:11:30.299 --> 00:11:36.800
is that we know Jaqen can look like Arya,
and that Jaqen will die for Arya – so maybe

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:41.480
he’s doing it again – dying in Arya’s
place so that the real Arya can escape.

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:45.360
This would explain a lot because the Arya
of this episode acts really different to the

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:46.929
Arya of last episode.

00:11:46.929 --> 00:11:49.629
Last episode, Arya hides out, with her sword
drawn.

00:11:49.629 --> 00:11:53.429
It looks like she knows she’s being hunted
by assassins, and she’s taking it seriously.

00:11:53.429 --> 00:11:58.779
But this episode, Arya wanders about in the
open, not paying attention to her surroundings.

00:11:58.779 --> 00:12:02.160
She seems to have found the time for a haircut
and a new outfit, and she doesn’t even have

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:03.559
her sword at her belt.

00:12:03.559 --> 00:12:04.559
She walks different.

00:12:04.559 --> 00:12:05.559
She talks different.

00:12:05.559 --> 00:12:08.600
She uses her right hand when Arya is left-handed.

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:13.939
Everything about her is off – so maybe she’s
not Arya, but Jaqen, pretending to be Arya.

00:12:13.939 --> 00:12:17.740
The really difficult question is – why would
Jaqen do this?

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:19.990
Why die in Arya’s place?

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:24.380
Maybe what’s going on here is that this
is all a test of the waif – cause she’s

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:27.770
been a pretty rubbish Faceless Man lately
– she’s meant to be “no one”, with

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:33.179
no desires, no personality, just pure obedience
– but she clearly enjoys tormenting Arya,

00:12:33.179 --> 00:12:35.109
she clearly wants to kill her.

00:12:35.109 --> 00:12:38.484
Jaqen tells her not to let Arya suffer, and
yet the waif stabs Arya – or who she thinks

00:12:38.484 --> 00:12:41.709
is Arya – in the gut so she dies slowly
and painfully.

00:12:41.709 --> 00:12:46.300
The waif is failing her training, so maybe
Jaqen arranged all this to fuck with her somehow.

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:50.100
It’s hard to guess at the specifics – maybe
we’ll just have to wait and see.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:54.629
Either way, it seems all but certain that
Arya will survive this.

00:12:54.629 --> 00:12:58.329
Back in the riverlands, the Hound finds that
Ray and his people have been slaughtered,

00:12:58.329 --> 00:13:00.720
presumably by these guys from the brotherhood.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.920
And this is a pretty crazy thing, we’ve
never seen the brotherhood do anything this

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:07.980
bad before, and from the looks of the food
on the ground, they don’t even do it for

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:08.980
supplies.

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:09.980
So, why?

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.970
The fact that Ray is hanged might be a hint.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:16.559
Cause in the books, the brotherhood really
starts to go downhill when their original

00:13:16.559 --> 00:13:21.690
leader Beric dies, and is replaced by a new
leader, called Lady Stoneheart . We won’t

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:26.049
spoil who Stoneheart is, cause she might still
appear in the show eventually, but she is

00:13:26.049 --> 00:13:29.749
called the Hangwoman for her habit of hanging
her enemies.

00:13:29.749 --> 00:13:35.329
Stoneheart leads the brotherhood down a dark,
violent path so maybe she’s involved here?

00:13:35.329 --> 00:13:39.379
But as far as we’ve seen even she will only
kill the guilty, we’ve never seen her massacre

00:13:39.379 --> 00:13:40.429
whole villages…

00:13:40.429 --> 00:13:44.329
So basically we don’t know why the brotherhood
would do this.

00:13:44.329 --> 00:13:48.110
What we do know is that Sandor’s coming
for them – he takes up his axe and goes

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:51.459
after the brotherhood, which probably won’t
go well for them.

00:13:51.459 --> 00:13:54.970
It’s gonna be awesome to see how Sandor’s
involved in the story ahead.

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:57.059
He might meet Brienne again round Riverrun.

00:13:57.059 --> 00:14:00.430
He might reunite with Arya when she returns
to Westeros.

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.189
He might meet Sansa again.

00:14:02.189 --> 00:14:05.009
And maybe Sandor will meet his brother.

00:14:05.009 --> 00:14:09.679
Sandor and Gregor Clegane have the angriest,
bloodiest sibling rivalry in all of Game of

00:14:09.679 --> 00:14:13.549
Thrones, Gregor was the one who burned Sandor’s
face, back in the day.

00:14:13.549 --> 00:14:18.720
They’ve both come a long way since – Sandor
almost dies and rises as a changed man, and

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:22.799
Gregor dies and is resurrected as a silent
giant zombie.

00:14:22.799 --> 00:14:27.769
There is a theory – that if Gregor represents
Cersei in her trial by combat, the Faith will

00:14:27.769 --> 00:14:33.239
be represented by Sandor – so the brothers
Clegane, two of the most powerful warriors

00:14:33.239 --> 00:14:37.850
in Westeros, will fight before all King’s
Landing, in the biggest most spectacular clash

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.850
in the series.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:56.389
This theory is called Cleganebowl.

00:14:56.389 --> 00:15:06.730
&lt;hype&gt;
Thank you for watching, and thank you to all

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:11.499
Patrons for supporting this channel, including
Jason A. Diegmueller, Jason Pan, Sandeep Rath,

00:15:11.499 --> 00:15:15.259
Ken Gray, Adam Allidina, Jessica Stone-Weaver,
and Terd_Furgeson.

00:15:15.259 --> 00:15:16.160
Cheers.

